reated_at":"2016-06-03T11:46:13Z","updated_at":"2016-06-03T11:46:13Z","body":"> The Plunker doesn't contain a custom exception handler. Is that intentional?\n\nYes. Though implementing a custom exception handler is my final goal, I just wondered why only the first exception is logged by the default exception handler?\n\n> I guess this is what you want http://plnkr.co/edit/zbzllPKzAd7T0AQp22Id?p=preview\n\nIn the end it is, but I wasn't able to do so yet, because I'm getting a TypeScript transpile error:\n\n> Class 'MyExceptionHandler' incorrectly implements interface 'ExceptionHandler'. \n> Property '_logger' is missing in type 'MyExceptionHandler'.\n\nThanks to your example I found out that my tries of implementing a custom handler would have worked with TypeScript 1.7, but not with TypeScript 1.8 (which is used by angular-cli), which leaves me in the weird situation in which I can't use angular-cli when I want to make something which uses a custom exception handler. At least I currently can't see a way…\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/223558457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"PhilippSoehnlein","id":242837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MjgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilippSoehnlein","html_url":"https://github.com/PhilippSoehnlein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilippSoehnlein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilippSoehnlein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilippSoehnlein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilippSoehnlein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilippSoehnlein/subscriptions","organizations_ur